content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-201 — Velatek VX-90 dosing pump, serial VX-5531. Reported diaphragm/head chemical leak at approximately 2 drops per second; motor running normally.",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Leak reading: approximately 2 drops per second at the diaphragm/head. Applicable documented limit: none—no Velatek VX-90 allowable leakage, alarm or shutdown limit is supplied. The HF-300 manual provides bearing-housing temperature limits only (normal up to 70°C, alarm 80°C, trip 90°C), not a diaphragm-leak limit, and those data are for a different pump. P1 and immediate stopping are therefore conservative interim responses to an active chemical release, not classifications against a documented VX-90 threshold.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Motor reading: 'running normally' is qualitative; no current, speed, vibration or bearing temperature was measured. Applicable documented limit: none for P-201. The site immediate-stop rule concerns vibration in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, which has not been reported, and its bearing-temperature P1 rule requires temperature above the manufacturer's alarm limit, also not reported. The HF-300 temperature values cannot be used as P-201 limits.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Most likely is a failed or damaged diaphragm at the liquid head, because the report specifically identifies the diaphragm as leaking; the head sealing interface should also be checked during the correctly documented strip-down. This remains an inspection hypothesis. The HF-300 troubleshooting entry for shaft-seal leakage, seal faces and shaft misalignment does not diagnose this Velatek diaphragm/head leak.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop P-201 and prevent its return to service while the active chemical leak is assessed and repaired. This is a precautionary planning decision, not an assertion that SSP-07's highest-severity-zone vibration stop criterion has been met.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before opening the pump head for diaphragm work, electrically isolate and apply lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, and mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves. SSP-07 Rev 3 applies to all site pumps, and these controls apply to work inside a pump or on its seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drain and vent first, then obtain a line-break permit before opening the head. Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves for work on the chemically dosed line; treat these as minimum controls pending identification of the chemical and any additional chemical-specific requirements.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before any lifting operation, verify the actual component weight. For any component heavier than 25 kg, obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment. Do not assume the 68 kg HF-300 back-pull-out assembly mass applies to P-201.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Place disassembly on technical-documentation hold until the Velatek VX-90 procedure and correct parts are available. Do not substitute the HF-300 back-pull-out/mechanical-seal procedure, HF3-series parts or HF-300 tightening torques. Under the correct VX-90 procedure, inspect the diaphragm and head sealing surfaces and replace confirmed failed components; VX-90 torque values are presently unavailable.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Close-out remains blocked until VX-90 reassembly and leak/function-test acceptance criteria are supplied. Record the post-repair leak rate and test result against those criteria; do not borrow HF-300 procedures or torque values for acceptance.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC are required before work inside the pump or on its seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanically isolate both suction and discharge valves before pump-head work.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "A line-break permit is required; drain and vent before line breaking.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are required for work on chemically dosed lines. Additional PPE, decontamination and spill controls cannot be specified until the chemical is identified.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If any component to be lifted is heavier than 25 kg, a shift-supervisor-signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment are required; the weight must first be confirmed for this Velatek pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The AquaDyne HF-300 O&M information is not an alternative repair specification for P-201. Its 68 kg assembly mass, temperature limits, HF3-series parts, mechanical-seal procedure and Table 5 torques belong to the HF-300, whereas this asset is a Velatek VX-90, serial VX-5531. None of those equipment-specific values is carried into this work order.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "There is an HF-300 torque conflict, but it does not produce an applicable P-201 torque. Table 5 lists 25 Nm for M10 seal-gland nuts. Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, supersedes that arrangement only for HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above: use HF3-450B and 30 Nm. Pumps below HF3-22000 continue with HF3-450 and Table 5. VX-5531 is outside both HF-300 serial populations, so neither 25 Nm nor 30 Nm, neither seal part, nor the bulletin’s 0.1 mm sleeve-scoring criterion governs this repair.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The sodium-hypochlorite statement is limited to filtered-water pumps P-101 through P-106 and therefore does not identify P-201's chemical. The generic SSP-07 requirement for goggles and nitrile gloves still applies to chemically dosed-line work, but no sodium-hypochlorite-specific assumption is made.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What chemical is being pumped, including concentration and SDS requirements, and what additional PPE, spill containment, decontamination and waste-disposal controls are required?",
    "What are the Velatek VX-90 diaphragm/head disassembly and reassembly procedure, fastener torques, inspection limits, allowable leakage criterion and post-repair test requirements?",
    "What are the correct diaphragm and any head-seal/gasket or associated component part numbers, quantities and material-compatibility requirements for serial VX-5531?",
    "Are there Velatek service bulletins or serial/date-dependent changes applicable to VX-5531?",
    "What are the weights of any components requiring lifting, so the greater-than-25 kg lifting controls can be confirmed?",
    "What site chemical-leak procedure and priority matrix apply? Confirm the emergency/spill classification, final priority and shutdown requirement; P1 and immediate stopping are interim conservative choices because the chemical and VX-90 leak limit are unknown.",
    "What trade, crew size, labour duration and spare-parts lead time are required? The supplied evidence provides no VX-90 labour estimate or parts availability."
  ]
}
